AD  - Ontario Ministry of the Environment and Climate Change, Toronto, ON, Canada
AD  - Environment and Climate Change Canada, Ottawa, ON, Canada
AD  - Senior Scientific Advisor on Air Quality, Ontario Ministry of the Environment and Climate Change, 125 Resources Road, Etobicoke, M9P 3V6, ON, Canada
AB  - The Federal Equivalent Method SHARP 5030 has been employed since 2013 at 40 stations across Ontario, Canada to continuously monitor ambient levels of fine particulate matter. Integrated samplers were collocated with the SHARP 5030 at six select stations to collect 24-hr integrated air samples. Concurrent measurements of the SHARP 5030 and the integrated samplers provide a unique opportunity to assess the field operation performance for the SHARP 5030 in Ontario. Data comparison showed that measurements by the SHARP 5030 were generally comparable to those by the integrated samplers including the Federal Reference Method (FRM), the dichotomous (Dichot) sampler, and the Speciation samplers. The FRM results show that the slope and intercept met the acceptance limits for PM2.5 Class III Federal Equivalent Method (FEM) Designation for 2013, Spring and Fall. The ratio of FEM/FRM was 1.0 or 1.1. Twenty-four-hour averages of the SHARP 5030 correlated well with the collocated Dichot and Speciation results. The differences between SHARP 5030 and 24-hour integrated results were found larger at low PM2.5 levels, but not dependant on seasons. Three years of PM2.5 continuous measurements in Ontario showed good reliability of the SHARP 5030 as indicated by average 98% valid data reported to the public. © 2017 Air and Waste Management Association. All Rights Reserved.
